---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Bodily Sovereignty">
 

  <Header />

  <main id="top">
    <!-- HERO  -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="layered-heading">
          <span class="bg-blackletter" aria-hidden="true">
            Bodily<br />Sovereignty
          </span>
          <h1 class="fg-serif">
            Bodily<br />Sovereignty
          </h1>
        </div>

        <p class="hero-tagline">We need to appreciate our women more.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- MARY SHELLEY SECTION -->
    <section id="shelley" class="editorial-band band-sage">
      <div class="band-inner">
        <h2 class="band-title">
          <span>Mary</span>
          <span>Shelley</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="band-copy">
          Shelley grew up without a mother leaving her to navigate a world that
          does not like independent women alone. Following this her life was
          full of grief, including the loss of three children and the drowning
          of her husband. On top of this, she was not credited for her writing
          initially since it was acceptable for women to be writers. Despite
          all of these setbacks, she endured and became recognized as a
          brilliant writer, reshaping literature and philosophy. Ultimately,
          Frankenstein is a timeless tale when analyzed under a feminine lens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SUMITA KAUR SECTION -->
    <section id="kaur" class="editorial-band band-olive">
      <div class="band-inner">
        <h2 class="band-title">
          <span>Sumita</span>
          <span>Kaur</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="band-copy">
          Sumita Kaur’s 2025 essay argues that bodily autonomy is the foundation
          necessary for women’s empowerment. It is more than just reproductive
          rights; it is the right to self-sovereignty, freedom from cultural
          conditioning, and personal agency. Women are conditioned to feel that
          their bodies are not truly their own but something meant to be
          controlled. Victor views the natural world and his creation as objects
          to be manipulated but ultimately abandons them when they fail to
          conform to his expectations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONCLUSION SECTION -->
    <section id="conclusion" class="conclusion-band">
      <div class="conclusion-inner">
        <p>
          Mary Shelley’s life of profound grief and systemic marginalization
          directly informed Frankenstein, and when viewed through a modern
          feminist lens, the novel serves as an exploration of bodily autonomy,
          self-sovereignty, and the dangers of patriarchal control.
        </p>
        <p>
          Just as Shelley navigated a world hostile to independent women, the
          monster is brought into existence without consent and ultimately
          abandoned when he fails to conform to his creator’s expectations. Kaur
          connects this dynamic to the broader argument that true women’s
          empowerment requires total freedom from cultural conditioning and
          ownership over one’s own existence, drawing a direct parallel between
          Victor Frankenstein’s desire to conquer nature and society’s historic
          impulse to control women’s bodies and autonomy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --plum-dark: #381028;
    --plum-ink: #2b0917;
    --black-bg: #050505;
    --sage-bg: #466346;
    --olive-bg: #6a7b33;
    --off-white: #ecefe9;

    --font-gothic: "Manufacturing Consent", serif;
    --font-serif: "Libre Baskerville", serif;
    --font-sans: "DM Sans", sans-serif;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    background-color: var(--black-bg);
    color: var(--off-white);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  /* Header & Footer fallback/theme helpers */
  header,
  footer {
    background-color: var(--plum-dark);
    color: var(--off-white);
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* 1. Hero */
  .hero {
    background-color: var(--black-bg);
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 5rem)
      clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7.5rem);
  }

  .hero-inner {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .layered-heading {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7.5rem);
  }

  .bg-blackletter {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-gothic);
    font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 11.5vw, 10.5rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    color: var(--plum-dark);
    user-select: none;
  }

  .fg-serif {
    position: absolute;
    top: 32%;
    left: 23%;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.6vw, 3.3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: #ffffff;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .hero-tagline {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.1vw, 1.85rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* 2 & 3. Editorial Color Bands (Shelley & Kaur) */
  .editorial-band {
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 8.5rem) clamp(2rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }

  .band-sage {
    background-color: var(--sage-bg);
  }

  .band-olive {
    background-color: var(--olive-bg);
  }

  .band-inner {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .band-title {
    font-family: var(--font-gothic);
    font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 9vw, 8.2rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 0.94;
    color: var(--plum-ink);
  }

  .band-title span {
    display: block;
  }

  .band-copy {
    font-size: clamp(0.88rem, 1.05vw, 1rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--off-white);
    max-width: 43ch;
  }

  /* 4. Conclusion Section */
  .conclusion-band {
    background-color: var(--black-bg);
    padding: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 9rem) clamp(1.75rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }

  .conclusion-inner {
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(0.92rem, 1.1vw, 1.05rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--off-white);
  }

  /* Responsive Stacking */
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .band-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.25rem;
    }

    .fg-serif {
      left: 16%;
    }
  }
</style>